     "caption": "A rectangle of width 4 split into x and 3: area 4x + 12.",
     "alt": "A rectangle split into two parts with areas 4x and 12."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Substitution",
     "md": "Replace each letter by its value, keep brackets round negative numbers, then use BODMAS. If x = 3 and y = −2, then 2x² − y = 2 × 3² − (−2) = 18 + 2 = 20."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Adding unlike terms: 3a + 2b is **not** 5ab.\n- Expanding only the first term: 3(x + 4) is 3x + 12, not 3x + 4.\n- Writing x² as 2x: x² means x × x, so with x = 3 it is 9, not 6."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1: simplify and expand",
     "statement": "Simplify 4a + 3b − a + 2b, then expand 3(2x − 4).",
     "steps": [
      "Collect the a terms: 4a − a = 3a. Collect the b terms: 3b + 2b = 5b. So 3a + 5b.",
      "Expand: 3 × 2x = 6x and 3 × (−4) = −12, so 6x − 12."
     ],
     "answer": "**3a + 5b; 6x − 12**"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2: a rectangle",
     "statement": "A rectangular plot at Buea has length (x + 3) m and width 4 m. Write its area in expanded form and find it when x = 5.",
     "steps": [
      "Area = 4(x + 3) = 4x + 12.",
      "Substitute x = 5: 4 × 5 + 12 = 32.",
      "The area is 32 m²."
     ],
     "answer": "**4x + 12; 32 m²**",
