   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Equation",
     "md": "An **equation** states that two expressions are equal: 3x + 7 = 22. To **solve** it means finding the value of x that makes it true. We keep the equation balanced: whatever we do to one side we do to the other side."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Method",
     "md": "Use **inverse operations** to undo what has been done to x, in reverse order. 3x + 7 = 22: subtract 7 to get 3x = 15, then divide by 3 to get x = 5. Check: 3 × 5 + 7 = 22. With x on both sides, move the x terms to one side and the numbers to the other."
    },
